[ceiling] These flat undersides are the snap's withdrawal shoulders. Each needs a square bearing over the frame's 3 mm catch web so a downward pull does not cam the wing inward. The installed model provides 0.40 mm static allowance, including the supported-face allowance, beneath each 2.75 mm hook; it does not require that modeled gap to remain physically open under load. The hook tops retain 269.895 mm² of silicone bearing at Z306.05. The body-down print needs removable support beneath these horizontal shoulders, accessible past their outer edges before assembly. Current support placement, finish, removal effort, loaded retention and lifetime remain unqualified.
alternatives: Sloping the underside creates a release ramp under withdrawal. A corbel into the slot blocks the wing's insertion travel. Turning the cradle over puts support inside the elbow pocket. Keep the square shoulders and their accessible support requirement.
